r in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $\\omega$ be a complex number such that $|\\omega| = 1,$ and the equation\n\\[z^2 + z + \\omega = 0\\]has a pure imaginary root $z.$  Find $\\omega + \\overline{\\omega}.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"c83d3dd7a072b28821f82dffb8a2373b7db9dda307b025ed1c97d43a681622c4"},"seconds":36.602086544036865,"seed":117566502037160382,"stop":"eos","text":"Given that $\\omega$ is a complex number such that $|\\omega| = 1$, and the equation $z^2 + z + \\omega = 0$ has a pure imaginary root $z$, we can denote the pure imaginary root as $z = bi$ where $b \\in \\mathbb{R}$.\n\nFirst, substitute $z = bi$ into the given quadratic equation:\n\\[\n(bi)^2 + bi + \\omega = 0\n\\]\nSimplify the terms:\n\\[\n-b^2 + bi + \\omega = 0\n\\]\n\nSeparate the real and imaginary parts:\n\\[\n-b^2 + \\omega = 0 \\quad \\text{(real part)}\n\\]\n\\[\nbi = 0 \\quad \\text{(imaginary part)}\n\\]\n\nFrom the imaginary part, we have:\n\\[\nbi = 0 \\implies b = 0\n\\]\n\nHowever, this would imply that $z = 0$, which is not a pure imaginary number. Therefore, we need to consider the real and imaginary parts separately.\n\nFrom the real part:\n\\[\n-b^2 + \\omega = 0 \\implies \\omega = b^2\n\\]\n\nSince $|\\omega| = 1$, we must have:\n\\[\n|b^2| = 1 \\implies b^2 = 1 \\implies b = \\pm 1\n\\]\n\nThus, the pure imaginary roots are \\(z = i\\) or \\(z = -i\\). Let's verify each case:\n\n1. If \\(z = i\\):\n\\[\ni^2 + i + \\omega = 0 \\implies -1 + i + \\omega = 0 \\implies \\omega = 1 - i\n\\]\n\n2. If \\(z = -i\\):\n\\[\n(-i)^2 - i + \\omega = 0 \\implies -1 - i + \\omega = 0 \\implies \\omega = 1 + i\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\(\\omega + \\overline{\\omega}\\) for both cases:\n\n1. For \\(\\omega = 1 - i\\):\n\\[\n\\overline{\\omega} = 1 + i \\implies \\omega + \\overline{\\omega} = (1 - i) + (1 + i) = 2\n\\]\n\n2. For \\(\\omega = 1 + i\\):\n\\[\n\\overline{\\omega} = 1 - i \\implies \\omega + \\overline{\\omega} = (1 + i) + (1 - i) = 2\n\\]\n\nIn both cases, we find:\n\\[\n\\omega + \\overline{\\omega} = 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
